<title>USA: Wheeling-Pittsburgh denies NRLB complaint.</title>
<headline>Wheeling-Pittsburgh denies NRLB complaint.</headline>
<dateline>WHEELING, W.Va. 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>WHX Corp unit Wheeling-Pittsburgh Steel Corp said that it denies that it has failed to comply with the National Labor Relations Act in dealing with the United Steelworkers of America.</p>
<p>The National Labor Relations Board issued a complaint against the company, but Wheeling-Pittsburgh said it will present evidence at a June 30 hearing that shows that the company provided the union with relevant financial information and that the company acted within its rights.  </p>
<p>Wheeling-Pittsburgh said it is appealing the National Labor Relations Board's dismissal of the company's charge that the union failed to bargain in good faith.</p>
<p>United Steelworkers of America employees at Wheeling-Pittsburgh have been on strike since October 1, 1996, a company spokesman said. The strike has affected 4,500 union members at the company's eight facilities in West Virginia, Ohio and Pennsylvania, the spokesman said.</p>
</text>
